WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.110
The John Wick series is a resounding success,
with Keanu Reeves bringing the retired assassin

00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:07.830
back for a third feature-length rampage.

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.680
There's no better time to break down how the
actor prepares to take on the physically demanding

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:12.180
role.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.280
You might be surprised at just how intensely
he works to become John Wick.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:21.160
While watching all the insane stunts he pulls
off in the John Wick films, it's important

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:23.900
to keep in mind that Keanu Reeves is in his
50s.

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:28.269
Yet he makes those moves look effortless,
and as often as they can get away with it,

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:30.019
yes, it's really him.

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:35.360
Reeves logged his first screen credit in 1984,
before many of his modern fans were even born.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:39.370
Since then, the man has given us decades of
badass characters, many of which helped prepare

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.040
him for his turn as John Wick.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:45.160
Understandably, he's starting to slow down
a bit as he gets older, but he still puts

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.310
everything he can into his performances.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:51.240
He mentioned in a profile in Men's Journal,
"I can't do stairs as fast.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.160
But if you say 'action,' I'll go."

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:54.320
"Yeah.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:56.120
I'm thinking I'm back!"

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.859
To prepare for playing John Wick, Reeves goes
through what he describes as a three-month

00:01:00.859 --> 00:01:04.809
"John Wick Boot Camp" to help get him ready
to take on the demanding role.

00:01:04.809 --> 00:01:09.720
The training regimen focuses on the character's
central concerns: fighting, driving, and guns.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:12.000
"Lots of guns."

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.180
Reeves talked about the routine in an interview
with Page Six, revealing how he sharpens his

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.210
shooting skills before the cameras roll.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.060
As he described it,

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.800
Reeves said he loves playing and training
for the role, adding that he couldn't wait

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.460
to return for a third installment.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.740
Reeves said of Wick as a character,

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.100
"You working?"

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:51.160
"...Yeah."

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.299
One defining characteristic of the John Wick
films is how effortlessly Keanu Reeves carries

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.720
himself around firearms.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:02.140
He always seems totally in control, utilizing
the smallest amount of energy possible in

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:03.560
order to take out his foes.

00:02:03.800 --> 00:02:08.240
There isn't a lot of film trickery involved
in his technique it's mostly just Keanu being

00:02:08.260 --> 00:02:10.500
really, really good at handling guns.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:15.220
In order to prepare for playing an expert
assassin, Reeves works with shooting ace Taran

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:19.120
Butler, a world champion in many shooting
competitions who's served as a consultant

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.750
for several different television and film
productions and appeared on competitive shooting

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.290
shows like Top Shot and Impossible Shots.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.500
In his John Wick training, Reeves has spent
time with Butler at Taran Tactical Innovations,

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.540
a training ground for competitive shooters.

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.220
If Chapter 2 is anything to go by, we can
expect the gunplay to get amped up even more

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:37.360
in John Wick 3.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.660
John Wick also possesses some seriously impressive
driving skills, which is something else Keanu

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:44.680
Reeves practices in his preparation for the
role.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:49.440
Because of the degree of difficulty involved
in some of the set pieces, stunt driver Jeremy

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:53.890
Fry handles the more dangerous tasks, like
pulling off the "flying drift" maneuver in

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:54.600
the second film.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:59.080
However, a big part of Reeves' "boot camp"
also includes working with stuntmen to improve

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.600
his own driving skills for scenes behind the
wheel.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:05.940
The fancy driving comes pretty naturally to
Reeves, who's a bit of an aficionado in the

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:07.300
realm of luxury vehicles.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.020
He's been known to own a Porsche and several
impressive motorcycles.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:15.440
In past films, he's sat behind the wheel of
Ferraris, Mustangs, and some impressive muscle

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.260
cars of the '60s and '70s.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:22.540
Reeves' trainers claim that his driving significantly
improved from the first John Wick to the second.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.660
It seems logical that he'd continue driving
circles around everyone in Chapter 3.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:31.580
One of the biggest problems with many modern
action films lies in the editing of fight

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.580
sequences.

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.790
Whether it's to hide the fact that the actors
can't really fight or not, many fight scenes

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:40.290
today get edited to the point where it's impossible
to tell what's happening.

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:44.310
But Reeves' impressive martial arts résumé
helps the filmmakers he works with craft much

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:48.260
more impressive fight scenes by allowing them
to use long cuts and show techniques that

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.220
other movies can't.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:55.200
Reeves trained in multiple different disciplines
to perfect the fighting style John Wick uses.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.120
Jiu-jitsu, judo, and practical grappling techniques
are all mixed in with extensive gun practice

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.000
to make Wick's abilities look effortless.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:05.920
The care Reeves takes to get the moves right
helps to save on money, time, and editing

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:06.780
decisions later on.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:11.560
Director Chad Stahelski, spoke about the production's
approach in the lead-up to Chapter 2, saying,

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:20.780
Keanu Reeves' workout routine for John Wick
serves a dual purpose.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:24.580
For one, it's tailor-made for Wick's no-nonsense,
explosive fighting style.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:28.840
His character needs ruthless efficiency, not
bulging muscles, so his workout is grounded

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:29.970
in that philosophy.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:33.850
On the other hand, Reeves is in his 50s, so
his workout is tailored more to strengthen

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.340
his joints and core muscle groups and have
them working in harmony.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:41.230
Reeves' trainer, Patrick Murphy, has said
that the John Wick workout mostly utilizes

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:45.060
resistance bands in place of free weights,
because they're easier on the joints and help

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:46.540
the body learn more control.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:50.440
He spoke about the routine with Muscle and
Fitness, saying that the focus was on, quote,

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:05.280
Part of John Wick's massive success is due
to its amazingly choreographed and performed

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.440
action sequences.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:11.020
They often read like dance sequences, and
a big part of that is Reeves' focus on nailing

00:05:11.020 --> 00:05:13.200
the moves before the cameras ever roll.

